{"id":"city-landlords","title":"Who the City rents from","question":"Which landlords hold the most City leases and floor area, and do any of them also appear in lobbying or campaign-donation records?","finding":"The Real Estate Division’s report of April 2025 lists 128 leases with the City as tenant, from 100 named landlords (1 with no landlord named), covering 4,641,796 square feet where an area is given; 62% of that area is rented from other public bodies. Among the 79 private and nonprofit landlords, Trinity Center LLC has the most leases (3) and Hudson Pacific Properties -Hudson 1455 Market St. LLC the most floor area (157,154 square feet). 8 private landlord names match a lobbyist client or a campaign-donation record exactly: 200 Paul LLC; 33 Gough LLC; 333 Valencia Owner LLC; The Salvation Army; 101 South Van Ness, LLC; Larkin Street Youth Services; HealthRight360; SF LGBT Community Center. The report gives no rents, so none are shown.","how":"The “City as tenant” sheet of the Real Estate Division’s lease report, grouped by landlord name as written (names identical after removing punctuation, spacing and company suffixes are merged). A landlord is marked a public body when its name contains a word such as Department, Port, Commission, Authority or District. Each name is then looked up, by exact name only (after removing punctuation and company suffixes), in this project’s lobbying file (clients of registered lobbyists that the City also pays) and its campaign-money file (City contractors named in contract-approval filings and donations by their listed officers; organizations that gave in their own name; donors’ employers). “City paid” is the lobbying file’s total of City payments to that name since fiscal 2019, for all purposes.","limits":"Renting to the City, lobbying and donating are disclosed; a match shows that one name appears in two public records and nothing more. Matching is by exact name, so a landlord that lobbies or donates through a parent company, an affiliate or its owners is missed, and two unrelated bodies with one name would be wrongly joined. A landlord the report writes in two different ways is counted as two. The lobbying file holds only clients the City also pays, so a landlord that lobbies but is paid under another name is missed. The report has no rents, terms or dates; 6 of the 128 rows have no floor area, and the sheet mixes building leases with licences for antennas, cables, art and parking as published. It is one snapshot, April 2025. The project’s separate screen on rent counts leases the Board of Supervisors approved since 2014, a different list from this inventory.","tier":"OFFICIAL","columns":[{"k":"landlord","t":"Landlord, as the report names it","type":"org"},{"k":"kind","t":"Kind","type":"text"},{"k":"leases","t":"Leases","type":"int"},{"k":"area","t":"Floor area, square feet","type":"int"},{"k":"departments","t":"City tenant","type":"text"},{"k":"addresses","t":"Address","type":"text"},{"k":"uses","t":"Use","type":"text"},{"k":"match","t":"Same name in lobbying or donation records","type":"text"},{"k":"lobbyContacts","t":"Lobbying contacts","type":"int"},{"k":"paidToLobbyists","t":"Paid to lobbyists","type":"usd"},{"k":"donations","t":"Donation records","type":"int"},{"k":"donationTotal","t":"Donations, dollars","type":"usd"},{"k":"cityPaid","t":"City paid this name since fiscal 2019","type":"usd"}],"rows":[{"landlord":"200 Paul LLC","landlordKey":null,"kind":"Private owner","leases":1,"area":53934,"departments":"Department of Technology","addresses":"200 Paul","uses":"Vehicle radio installation/repair shop/office","lobbyContacts":21,"paidToLobbyists":10000,"cityPaid":11284500,"donations":null,"donationTotal":null,"match":"Lobbyist client under this exact name: 21 recorded contacts with officials, 2012 to 2014, mostly about planning and building permits; $10,000 paid to lobbyists"},{"landlord":"33 Gough LLC","landlordKey":null,"kind":"Private owner","leases":1,"area":49000,"departments":null,"addresses":"33 Gough","uses":"Navigation Center","lobbyContacts":2,"paidToLobbyists":1020,"cityPaid":9750157,"donations":null,"donationTotal":null,"match":"Lobbyist client under this exact name: 2 recorded contacts with officials, 2016 to 2018, mostly about planning and building permits; $1,020 paid to lobbyists"},{"landlord":"333 Valencia Owner LLC","landlordKey":null,"kind":"Private owner","leases":1,"area":44229,"departments":null,"addresses":"333 Valencia","uses":"Office and Public facilities","lobbyContacts":4,"paidToLobbyists":812,"cityPaid":21709354,"donations":null,"donationTotal":null,"match":"Lobbyist client under this exact name: 4 recorded contacts with officials, 2018 to 2018, mostly about planning and building permits; $812 paid to lobbyists"},{"landlord":"The Salvation Army","landlordKey":"SALVATION ARMY","kind":"City-funded organization","leases":1,"area":10833,"departments":null,"addresses":"1156 Valencia","uses":"Shelter Facility for homeless","lobbyContacts":7,"paidToLobbyists":81318,"cityPaid":53256238,"donations":null,"donationTotal":null,"match":"Lobbyist client under this exact name: 7 recorded contacts with officials, 2021 to 2023, mostly about planning and building permits; $81,318 paid to lobbyists. Its staff are named as donors to 16 campaign committees, $4,270"},{"landlord":"101 South Van Ness, LLC","landlordKey":null,"kind":"Private owner","leases":1,"area":10469,"departments":"Reproduction & Mail, GSA","addresses":"110 12th","uses":"Reproduction & Mail Services","lobbyContacts":null,"paidToLobbyists":null,"cityPaid":null,"donations":7,"donationTotal":3500,"match":"Named as a City contractor in a contract-approval filing; 7 campaign donations by people listed as its officers, $3,500 in all, 339 to 346 days from the approval"},{"landlord":"Larkin Street Youth Services","landlordKey":"LARKIN STREET YOUTH SERVICES","kind":"City-funded organization","leases":1,"area":3300,"departments":"Human Services Agency","addresses":"538 Holloway